Qore OpenLDAP module packages
============================

This is a development snapshot for qore-testing, not a final release.
The runtime includes the native module, six source/AOT helpers, compiler
metadata and seven qldap tools with manual pages. Documentation includes
seven HTML references and local test fixtures. No LDAP server is installed
or started by the runtime package; SASL mechanism plugins are recommended.

Build with dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc and the matching Qore 3 SDK. Distribution
OpenLDAP and Cyrus SASL development packages are required. Offline full,
arch-only, indep-only, nocheck and nodoc profiles are supported; cross builds
require a separate host SDK and are rejected. AOT trailers are retained.
The source distribution offers MIT or LGPL licensing; Debian selects MIT.
The +ds source repack excludes only m4/acx_pthread.m4, an unused legacy
Autoconf macro with no accompanying license notice. Licensed Autoconf macros
remain included with their original notices.

Tests create a private, unprivileged loopback slapd with a fresh database,
synthetic credentials and an ephemeral TLS certificate. The fixture preflights
DIGEST-MD5/CRAM-MD5 SASL using the disposable directory's test users. These
mechanisms and permissive fixture access rules exist solely for tests.
No host LDAP configuration, external service or real account is used.
Installed runtime and fresh qcc tests exclude checkout module paths.
CLI checks cover help, real authentication with redacted verbose output and
verified StartTLS. Transaction commit/abort and control-value ownership are
covered against the local server; capability detection uses RootDSE rather
than swallowing client errors. Full GSSAPI/Kerberos, Active Directory and deployment
policies require separate environments and qualification.

Before general publication, qualify other Debian/Ubuntu releases and
architectures, freeze the Qore ABI and test relevant upgrades. No previous
binary module package is available for upgrade testing. Testing PPA publication
requires a matching published Qore SDK, source signing and upload.
